## 1. Android Developers - Create and Use Variables in Kotlin

This resource was used to understand:

- `val` and `var`
- Kotlin data types
- `Double`
- String values
- Boolean values
- Type inference
- String templates
- Basic variable operations

Reference:

https://developer.android.com/codelabs/basic-android-kotlin-compose-variables


## 2. Android Developers - Create and Use Functions in Kotlin

This resource was used to understand:

- Function declarations
- Function calls
- Parameters
- Arguments
- Return values
- Function signatures
- Default arguments
- Reusable functions

Reference:

https://developer.android.com/codelabs/basic-android-kotlin-compose-functions

## 3. Kotlin Documentation

This resource provides general information about Kotlin syntax, types, functions, variables, and programming concepts.

Reference:
https://developer.android.com/codelabs

## 4. Android Developers - Kotlin for Android

This resource provides background information about using Kotlin for Android development.

Reference:

https://developer.android.com/kotlin

---

## Purpose of the References

These resources were used as learning materials while completing the exercises in the portfolio.

The portfolio source code represents my completed learning activities, while the references provide additional explanations and official documentation for the Kotlin concepts used.
